course: dictionary
lesson: 2423
title: Words from music and stories
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cymbal is a round, flat plate of metal that makes a loud, ringing crash when you hit it with a stick or clash it against another cymbal. Context helps you see what it means. In «the Chinese lion dance two dancers play one lion, moving to drums and cymbals», drums and cymbals are things that make music, so cymbals must be instruments.
explain: Sometimes the sentence gives you a clue about the sound. Paul wrote that without love a person is only «a clanging cymbal», however great their gifts and knowledge. A clanging cymbal makes a loud, harsh noise, and Paul is saying that noise alone is not enough.
explain: Musicians use special words too. A «crash cymbal» is hit once to make a big sound, and to «clash the cymbals» means to bang two of them together. A hi-hat is a pair of cymbals on a drum kit, and the drummer opens and closes them with the foot.
fact: A cymbal is a round, flat plate of metal used as a musical instrument.
fact: «Cymbals» belong to the percussion family, the instruments you hit to make a sound.
fact: To «clash the cymbals» means to hit two of them together to make a loud ringing crash.
fact: A «hi-hat» is a pair of cymbals on a drum kit, worked with the foot.
fact: In the Bible (Psalm 150), people praise God with loud cymbals.
exercise: What is a cymbal? | A small wooden box you sit on | *A round, flat metal plate that makes a loud ringing crash | A long pole used for jumping | A bird that sings at dawn
exercise: On a drum kit, what is a hi-hat? | A bell that rings at the door | *A pair of cymbals worked with the foot | A tall hat worn by the drummer | A drum you hit with a stick
exercise: «The band clashed the cymbals at the end of the parade, and the crowd cheered.» What does clashed the cymbals mean? | Count the beats quietly | Tune the cymbals to a low note | Put the cymbals away in their case | *Hit two cymbals together to make a crash
test: Paul wrote that without love a person is only «a clanging cymbal». What does this suggest? | A person who plays the cymbals beautifully in an orchestra | *A person who is loud and noisy but has nothing real to offer | A person who is good at maths | A person who is very quiet and shy
test: How many dancers play one lion in the Chinese lion dance? | One | *Two | Five | Ten
exam: Which word in «two dancers play one lion, moving to drums and cymbals, sometimes jumping on poles» names an instrument? | dancers | poles | lion | *cymbals
